            "description": "Watch Corinthians vs Penarol highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 1, 2026. The lights of the CONMEBOL Libertadores shone brightly over the pitch on May 1, 2026 , as two of South America's historic giants locked horns in a high-stakes continental encounter. This clash between Corinthians and Penarol promised intensity and drama from the opening whistle, with both sides desperate to assert their dominance in the group stage. Early Dominance at the Arena The home side wasted little time in making their intentions clear, asserting control over the football match from the very first whistle. The breakthrough arrived in the 11th minute when Rodrigo Garro delivered a pinpoint ball into the danger zone, finding Gustavo Henrique . The defender rose to the occasion, meeting the delivery with precision to slot home the opening goal and send the home crowd into a frenzy. This early strike forced Penarol to rethink their defensive shell, but the Brazilian giants continued to hunt for more. As the first half progressed, the pressure became relentless. In the 25th minute, Yuri Alberto turned provider, carving out a chance with a clever assist that found Jesse Lingard in a pocket of space. The high-profile player showed his class with a clinical finish, doubling the lead and giving Corinthians a comfortable cushion. The movement between the front line was too much for the visitors to handle, as the quick passing sequences left the Uruguayan defense searching for answers. Tactical Adjustments and Rising Tension The second half saw a shift in momentum as Penarol attempted to claw their way back into the contest. Managerial changes began in the 57th minute when Gaston Togni was replaced by Luis Angulo , signaling a more offensive approach from the visitors. However, the sports drama intensified not through goals, but through a series of physical challenges. Facundo Alvez was shown a yellow card in the 68th minute for a late challenge, followed shortly by his teammate Jesus Trindade , who also entered the referee's book in the 76th minute as frustrations began to boil over. Corinthians remained disciplined, making several substitutions to freshen up their ranks and see out the result. Kaio came on for Andre Luiz just after the hour mark, while veteran Andre Carrillo and Zakaria Labyad were introduced in the 80th minute to provide stability in the midfield. Despite a late flurry of changes from Penarol , including the introduction of Abel Hernandez and Kevin Rodriguez , the Brazilian defense remained organized and resolute against the aerial bombardment. Closing the Door on the Continental Stage In the final minutes of the match , the hosts managed the clock with professional precision. The goalscoring hero Jesse Lingard received a standing ovation as he made way for Pedro Raul in the 88th minute, while Yuri Alberto was replaced by Vitinho to see out the remaining seconds. The referee’s final whistle after four minutes of stoppage time confirmed a professional performance from the home side, marking a significant step in their continental campaign and leaving the visitors to reflect on a difficult night in Brazil."
